    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **259 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including both new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe endpoint is served through OfficeFloor function injection with DTOs generated from an OpenAPI spec, so I threaded `registrationDate` through the whole stack:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, this makes the field both a create-time input and a response field, and `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` in the DTOs \u2014 which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter (MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically).\n\n3. **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` (the server's current date) when the client didn't supply one; a supplied date flows through untouched.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required; I updated all four for consistency.\n\nThe `PUT` path (`ApplyOwner`) deliberately doesn't touch `registrationDate`, so updates preserve the original registration date rather than clobbering it. The single `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler` line in the log is from an existing negative-path repository test (an intentional foreign-key violation), not a failure.",
